  "Question": "Square \\(ABCD\\) has side length \\(8\\). Point \\(E\\) lies on \\(BC\\) with \\(CE=6\\), and \\(P\\) is a moving point on diagonal \\(AC\\). Find the minimum value of \\(PB+PE\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "10",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(B\\) and \\(D\\) are reflections of each other across \\(AC\\), so \\(PB=PD\\). Thus, \\(PB+PE=PD+PE\\geq DE\\), and \\(DE=\\sqrt{8^2+6^2}=10\\).",
